Okay, the problem here is not that the game is unrealistic in this
case, but that there's a bug.  Y'see, to handle carrying over the normal
amount of weight, the game gives you a move, then waits a certain amount
of turns (dependent on weight) before giving you another one.  So if
you're burdened, it would be move-pause-move-pause-move-pause.  And if
you're overloaded, it's something like move-pause-pause-pause... etc.
So, the problem is that you moved (got the corpse), and during those
pauses an ape appeared and whacked you.  Then, you got your next move,
and dropped the corpse.  However, since it doesn't check to see your 
weight status until the next turn, you still had to wait through those
pauses from being overloaded!  R.I.P.

